{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793198794,"nonce":"Ah065Y5xJuvjkG4KlzGXeogq8Ac=","message":"Implementation and normal checks are complete. Layer samples now record self-contained destination geometry through the same helper as ordered images, selecting the active static/motion/composite/foreground command owner. The ordered walker retains completed output textures for referenced names, including effects and source opacity, and replays samples in order using existing image shaders. Source coordinates are local to the named layer frame; destination metadata preserves transform, explicit opacity and clips. Missing/forward/out-of-output references draw nothing. Zero output clears the old name, duplicate names replace earlier output, and retained textures return to the pool at the end of the pass. Only referenced IDs cause named-output bakes; unsampled IDs retain the prior footprint and path. Sample nodes are boxed so ordinary ordered nodes do not grow to contain image metadata.\n\nFinal normal controls so far: 41 app tests (7 new sampling, 2 scratch fingerprints, 9 cross-stream, 10 effect group, 8 mixed boundaries, 5 foreground RGBA) and 37 GPU tests (3 new native sample, 7 ordered overlay unit, 22 RGBA, 5 foreground layer). This includes clear/overlay 1x/4x, static/dynamic/scratch/foreground/captured BG-FG, source crop/effects/alpha, clips/affine metadata, transparent offscreen margins/fractional coordinates, larger same-bucket pool priming, duplicate/zero/missing/forward names, no stale next-pass output, raw commands with no capture metadata, and canvas-group direct/compositor replay across opacity endpoints. Logs /private/tmp/blinc-named-{new-gpu,new-cpu,hash,overlay-cpu,rgba,foreground-cpu,cross,effects,boundary,images}.log. A compositor test target initially lacked COPY_DST; corrected before final successful controls. GPU tests use the consolidated integration target; an initial per-file target invocation was corrected.\n\nScope and costs: the pass retains one post-effect GPU output per completed referenced name until replacement or pass completion, approximately 4*w*h bytes per output in RGBA8, plus existing bake/effect intermediates. Each sample reuses the texture view and copies only geometry/clip metadata, with no CPU pixel readback or replay RGBA upload. Named output adds bake/straighten work when the layer was previously flattenable. The ordinary unnamed and unreferenced-ID paths keep their prior dispatch; no performance timing claim. LayerTextureCache already has a separate public named texture store, unused by native layer recording. The new owner-local outputs do not read, replace or clear that persistent unqualified store. Persistent or independent-pass name resolution is outside this scoped fix and remains in the parent.\n\nHost source API: LayerCommand::Sample adds optional paint metadata; direct Rust constructors must supply paint: None or captured metadata. DynamicImage/RetainedImage gain Debug to support command diagnostics. No shader, GPU instance/primitive, shared ClipPath or FFI layout changes. Final scoped clippy and seven new GPU cases in forced data-texture/restored-normal modes are in progress after the last cost guard. No broad gates, desktop input, push or publishing.","files":null}]}